        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables: par value, bond price, and modified duration\n    bonds = [\n        {\"par_value\": 25_000_000, \"price\": 105, \"modified_duration\": 7.9},\n        {\"par_value\": 25_000_000, \"price\": 100, \"modified_duration\": 8.5},\n        {\"par_value\": 20_000_000, \"price\": 95, \"modified_duration\": 6.3},\n        {\"par_value\": 30_000_000, \"price\": 87, \"modified_duration\": 10.2},\n    ]\n\n    # Calculate the collection's price value of a basis point\n    pvbp = sum(\n        bond[\"modified_duration\"]\n        * (bond[\"par_value\"] * bond[\"price\"] / 100)\n        * 0.0001\n        for bond in bonds\n    )\n\n    # Return the answer to one decimal place\n    return round(pvbp, 1)\n```",
